    <https://ns.webcivics.net/values/deonticStatus> <https://ns.webcivics.net/values/HeuristicDerived>;
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/curationStatus> <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/Proposed>.
<https://ns.webcivics.net/concept/act-sch-2-sec-167-2-ss-1> <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/asserts> <https://ns.webcivics.net/concept/act-sch-2-sec-167-2-ss-1-logic-deontic-1>.
<https://ns.webcivics.net/concept/act-sch-2-sec-167-2-ss-1-logic-deontic-1> a <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/LogicApplication>;
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/modality> <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/Deontic>;
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/operator> "Prohibit";
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/logicSummary> "Prohibition of inducing a consumer to acquire goods or services by representing a rebate, commission, or other benefit in return for assisting others.";
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/premiseText> "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person, in trade or commerce, induces a consumer to acquire goods or services by representing that the consumer will, after the contract for the acquisition of the goods or services is made, receive a rebate, commission or other benefit in return for:  (i) giving the person the names of prospective customers; or  (ii) otherwise assisting the person to supply goods or services to other consumers; and";
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/conclusionText> "Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—$1,100,000; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—$220,000.";
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/executionSurface> "modalities::logic::deontic";
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/confidence> 1.0000;
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/curationStatus> <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/Proposed>.
<https://ns.webcivics.net/concept/act-sch-2-sec-167-2-ss-1> <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/asserts> <https://ns.webcivics.net/concept/act-sch-2-sec-167-2-ss-1-logic-alleninterval-2>.
<https://ns.webcivics.net/concept/act-sch-2-sec-167-2-ss-1-logic-alleninterval-2> a <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/LogicApplication>;
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/modality> <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/AllenInterval>;
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/operator> "Temporal Containment";
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/logicSummary> "Temporal containment of induced consumer acquisition.";
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/premiseText> "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person, in trade or commerce, induces a consumer to acquire goods or services by representing that the consumer will, after the contract for the acquisition of the goods or services is made, receive a rebate, commission or other benefit in return for:  (i) giving the person the names of prospective customers; or  (ii) otherwise assisting the person to supply goods or services to other consumers; and";
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/conclusionText> "(b) the receipt of the rebate, commission or other benefit is contingent on an event occurring after that contract is made.";
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/executionSurface> "modalities::interval_reasoning";
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/confidence> 1.0000;
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/curationStatus> <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/Proposed>.
